    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d685">

                <pb facs="0807" n="705" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg705"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 4598/47–48.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Gregory to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San
                                Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-04-07"><hi rendition="#italic">April 7,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 66, Salvadorean series.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the department’s serial No.
                    19, dated March 19, 1908,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d685-f1"/> in which the flying of
                    foreign flags in Salvador is spoken of, I have the honor to forward herewith a
                    copy and translation of the executive order of February 1, 1908, upon this
                    matter.</p>
                <p>There has not been, however, any question of the right of consuls or of foreign
                    ships to display their national flag.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. H. Gregory</hi>,
                    Jr.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d685-a1.xml" xpointer="d685-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
